<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Harith Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Harith Muhammad was the Farighunid amir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guzgan">Guzgan</a>, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, in the late 10th century. A patron of learning, he was the dedicatee of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudud-al-alam">Hudud al-Alam</a>, an anonymous Persian geography of the known world completed in 982. His family married into the house of the Ghaznavid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabuktigin">Sabuktigin</a>.</p></div>
